NAME
    mem - hexdump a range of memory

SYNOPSIS
    mem <space> <addr> [<len>]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints <len> bytes (default 16) from <space> starting at <addr> as a
    classic hex + ASCII dump, 16 bytes per row. <space> is one of the names
    'spaces' lists. Addresses/lengths are hex (an optional 0x or $ prefix is
    fine either way).

EXAMPLES
    mem WRAM 0
    mem CpuBus 8000 64
